<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is Copyright Assignment?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>Transfer of copyright ownership from assignor to assignee under S18. Must comply with S19: written, signed, work identified, rights specified, duration, territory, consideration. Partial or complete. For <a href="/brand-copyright-registration">Brand Copyright Registration</a>, see our page.</p>
                    <p>S17: author is first owner. Freelancer who builds your software owns the copyright without assignment deed. S17(c): employer owns for employment works. For <a href="/statutory-audit">Statutory Audit</a>, see our page.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Copyright Assignment:</strong></p>
                    <ul><li><strong>S18/S19:</strong> Assignment framework. Written + signed. Work, rights, duration, territory, consideration mandatory</li><li><strong>Default 5 Years:</strong> S19(5): unspecified duration = 5 years. S19(4): unspecified territory = India only. Always specify</li><li><strong>S57 Moral Rights:</strong> Non-assignable. Author retains attribution + integrity. Clause to transfer = void</li><li><strong>S17(c):</strong> Employer owns for employment works. Does NOT apply to contractors/freelancers</li><li><strong>2012 Amendment:</strong> New medium not existing at assignment = excluded unless specifically mentioned</li><li><strong>Copyright Office:</strong> Optional registration. Prima facie evidence. Recommended for high-value IP</li></ul>

                </div>
            </div>
